UID:10008247-1792603800-1792607400@breadloafmountainzen.org
SUMMARY:Dharma Reflection by Eisho (online and in person)
DESCRIPTION:When: Every Wednesday evening from 5:30-6:30pm. \nWhere: In person: 76 Court Street in Middlebury or online via Zoom (for zoom link click here) \nDetails: This is a time to hear and discuss the benefits of Zen in our everyday lives. We begin with silent sitting\, then Zen teachers\, Zen students\, and guests offer their reflections for about 30 minutes. Community conversation about the talk follows. Please come for the entire time so we can give our discussion time some energy and attention. It’s an open session. Always free. \nJoin us for our next reflection led by Eisho \nSensei Eisho has been part of Bread Loaf Mountain Zen Community nearly since its inception\, and has served our local and online sangha with a steady\, warm and trustworthy hand and heart. He brings clear insight\, humility\, and attentive care to his teaching\, spiritual counseling\, and our temple’s rituals. His Zen journey began when he was quite young\, and over the years\, he has served professionally as a Buddhist prison chaplain in the UK\, and has maintained a committed life of practice\, study\, and service at society’s margins. Eisho carries a wealth of wisdom from the many teachers he has studied with and shares it freely. In addition to other gifts\, skills\, and talents\, he is a Hakomi therapist and cherishes his roles as a partner\, father\, and grandfather. \n  \n\n				Dana Donation (Optional)\n			\n					\n		    			\n		    			    \n		    			\n						\n\n    \n\n\n					\n		             \n 
URL:https://breadloafmountainzen.org/event/dharma-reflection-by-eisho-sinclair-2/2026-10-21/
LOCATION:Bread Loaf Mountain Zen Community\, 76 Court Street\, Middlebury\, VT\, 05753\, United States
CATEGORIES:Dharma Talk,Hybrid
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://breadloafmountainzen.org/wp-content/uploads/2024/03/Eisho.jpg
END:VEVENT
