SUMMARY:Dharma Talk So'on Dunworth (online and in person)
DESCRIPTION:When: Every Wednesday at 5:30pm Eastern Time \nWhere:\nIn person 76 Court Street Middlebury VT\nand online via Zoom (click here for the zoom link) \nDetails: This is a time to hear and discuss the benefits of Zen in our everyday lives. We begin with silent sitting\, then Zen teachers\, Zen students\, and guests offer their reflections for about 30 minutes. Community conversation about the talk follows. Please come for the entire time so we can give our discussion time some energy and attention. It’s an open session. Always free. \nJoin us for our next reflection led by So’on. This reflection offers a chance to deepen your understanding and practice of Zen in a warm and inviting community setting. \nRic So’on Dunworth became a formal student of Joshin Sensei in 2018. \nSo’on carries the Dharma name “Ancestor’s Warmth.” Prior to joining BLMZC he practiced for many years at Zen Mountain Monastery in the Catskill Mountains of New York State. His original Teacher was John Daido Loori\, Roshi and he brings their insights and warmth to the BLMZC community. He first received the precepts with Daido Roshi in May of 1995 on the day that Maezumi Roshi died in Japan. So’on is a retired Clinical Social Worker and spent most of his career at Rutland Regional Medical Center in Rutland\, VT. So’on is married with a son and two Grand-sons. \n\n				Dana Donation (Optional)
URL:https://breadloafmountainzen.org/event/dharma-talk-soon-dunworth-online-and-in-person/2026-10-28/
LOCATION:VT
CATEGORIES:Dharma Talk,In-person,Online
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://breadloafmountainzen.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/09/Ric-So-on-Dunworth-2.jpg
END:VEVENT
